    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const item = $input.first();\nconst binary = item.binary.data;\n\nconst base64 = binary.data;\nconst mimeType = binary.mimeType || \"image/jpeg\";\n\nreturn [{\n  json: {\n    ...item.json,\n    image_base64: base64,\n    image_mime_type: mimeType\n  },\n  binary: item.binary\n}];"
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        672,
        288
      ],
      "id": "3280cb00-e9a4-402d-a4d7-97e60e03d11e",
      "name": "Parse Code to convert into 64base"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=Identify the battery model in this label photo.",
        "messages": {
          "messageValues": [
            {
              "message": "=You are inspecting a photo of a laptop battery's label for a battery sales business in Pakistan. The photo may be clear, blurry, angled, or partially cut off.  Look at the image and extract any visible model number, part number, or barcode text on the label. Respond with ONLY a single JSON object \u2014 no explanation, no markdown fences.  JSON schema: {   \"extracted_text\": \"<all legible text found on the label, or null if none is legible>\",   \"likely_model\": \"<your best single guess at the battery model/part number, or null>\",   \"confidence\": <float 0.0-1.0, how confident you are the label is fully legible and correct>,   \"notes\": \"<one sentence: e.g. 'label partially obscured by glare' or 'clear, high-res label'>\" }  Rules: 1. Base confidence on image quality and label legibility, not on whether the model looks    \"familiar\" to you. A crisp photo of an unfamiliar code should still score high; a blurry    photo of a well-known code should score low. 2. If you can't make out any text at all, set extracted_text and likely_model to null and    confidence to 0.0 \u2014 do not guess. 3. Never invent or \"clean up\" characters you can't actually see. Report exactly what's    legible, even if it looks incomplete. 4. Output raw JSON only."
            },
            {
              "type": "HumanMessagePromptTemplate",
              "messageType": "imageBinary"
            }
          ]
        },
        "batching": {}
      },
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.chainLlm",
      "typeVersion": 1.9,
      "position": [
        896,
        288
      ],
      "id": "70ad9a37-3d69-4078-b414-822d61bca87d",
      "name": "LLM checking the confidence of pic + extracting data ",
      "retryOnFail": true,
      "notesInFlow": false,
      "onError": "continueErrorOutput"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const text = $json.text;\n\nconst result = JSON.parse(text);\n\nreturn [\n  {\n    json: {\n      ...$json,\n      output: result\n    }\n  }\n];"
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        1248,
        192
      ],
      "id": "bf0a973c-68a6-47e6-88f4-869e2a5b6570",
      "name": "Parse Code in js"
    },
